  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/trigonopoma-pauciperforatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Trigonopoma pauciperforatum (formerly Rasbora pauciperforata) usually grows up to 4 cm long (some literature says up to 7 cm). It looks like a twin species of the glow-light tetra (Hemigrammus erythrozonus) from the Essequibo River in Guyana, although the muzzle of T. pauciperforatum is much more pointed and the adipose fin is missing.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/trigonopoma-pauciperforatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Sundaland (Indonesia, Malay Peninsula), where it lives in black water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/trigonopoma-pauciperforatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>In the black water of Sundaland you will find many wonderful aquarium fish like chocolate gouramis, harlequin barbs and kuhli loaches. However, these are only the best known; the numerous species of small and colourful barbs and rasboras, for example, are only known by a few. Trigonopoma pauciperforatum is one of the prettiest of them.</p>"
    }
  ],
